EFFECT HOST APPLICATION SPECIFICATION
=====================================
Purpose: Recreate a desktop audio-effect host in Python 3. A pygame-only GUI
loads effect plugins from ./plugins, processes WAV files or live audio input,
and plays or saves the result. No tkinter.

1. Runtime and dependencies
---------------------------
- Python 3.9+
- Required: pygame, numpy
- Optional: sounddevice (audio input / live-through). If missing, the Audio
  Input dialog still opens and tells the user to pip install sounddevice.
- No scipy required in the host.

Layout of files:
  effects.py                 # this application
  plugins/*.py               # effect plugins (ignore _*.py)

2. Plugin discovery
-------------------
On startup, create ./plugins if needed. For each *.py that does not start
with "_":
  - Import via importlib.util.spec_from_file_location
  - Keep only classes defined in that module that expose:
      get_name, get_knobs, get_switches, apply_effect
  - Instantiate each matching class with no arguments.
Record failures (do not crash):
  - import / syntax errors
  - __init__ exceptions
  - file imported but no matching class
Each failure stores {file, reason, detail/traceback}.
If any failures exist, show PluginErrorDialog immediately. A "Plugin Errors"
button reopens it.

3. Window and layout
--------------------
- pygame.display.set_mode((980, 760), RESIZABLE)
- Caption: "Effect Host"
- 60 FPS loop
- On VIDEORESIZE, rebuild layout.
- Compute scale in [0.45, 1.0] so knobs, fonts, tabs, and the scope stay
  inside the window. Persist knob/switch/style values across relayout.
- Draw order (back to front): background, toolbar, tabs/dropdown header,
  status, active effect panel, main oscilloscope, plugin dropdown MENU
  (so it is never behind the panel), file dialog, error dialog, audio
  input dialog.

Colors (host chrome, RGB):
  BG (18,18,20), PANEL (30,30,34), PANEL_EDGE (70,70,78),
  TEXT (230,230,230), MUTED (160,160,168), BTN (55,55,62),
  BTN_HOT (80,80,92), BTN_ON (50,110,80), ACCENT (70,140,220),
  WARN (220,180,70), SCOPE_BG (8,16,12), SCOPE_GRID (20,50,28),
  SCOPE_TRACE (40,220,90)

4. Toolbar buttons (wrap to next row if needed)
-----------------------------------------------
Open WAV | Save WAV | Audio Input | Render | Play Processed | Repeat |
Original | Stop | [Plugin Errors if failures exist]

Prev / Next cycle the loaded plugin list.

5. Effect switching
-------------------
- 1..6 plugins: toggle tabs labeled with get_name(), in load order.
- More than 6 plugins: sorted dropdown (A-Z by get_name()). Draw the open
  list AFTER the effect panel. Up/Down opens and moves highlight; Enter
  selects and closes; Esc closes; mouse wheel scrolls.
- Left / Right (and comma / period) cycle load order.
- Only the ACTIVE effect is shown and applied on Render / Live Through.

6. Effect panel
---------------
One EffectPanel for the active plugin:
  - Rounded rectangle using plugin face/edge/text colors (see plugin spec).
  - Title = get_name()
  - Row of KnobWidgets (circle + needle + value + horizontal slider).
  - Optional StylePicker from getStyles()/get_styles().
      < 3 styles: always-visible list.
      >= 3 styles: dropdown.
  - Row of SwitchWidgets (pill + label).
Knobs/switches/style scale with window scale.

7. Knob widget
--------------
Size ~ 88 * scale (min 36). Sweep 225 deg down to -45 deg (270 deg).
Needle angle maps linearly min..max. Click points snap when within 3% of
span. Slider under the knob stays in sync. Colors: per-knob scheme if
present, else plugin theme knob_outline / knob_face / knob_needle.

8. Switch widget
----------------
Capsule ~44x22 * scale. On: switch_on. Off: switch_off. White/text dot
left=off, right=on. Click pill or label to toggle.

9. Style picker
---------------
getStyles() -> dict[str, int]. Keys are labels, values are ordinals.
Do NOT invent a Style knob. Attribute written is always effect.style as
int. Default selection: name whose value == getattr(effect, "style", None),
else first key. List colors from plugin style_* keys; if those keys are
absent from the theme overrides, use black background and yellow text.

10. Push settings before processing
-----------------------------------
For each knob: setattr(effect, sanitized_lower_name, value) AND
setattr(effect, original_name, value).
For each switch: same for bool.
If styles exist: effect.style = selected ordinal (int).
Then call apply_effect(audio, sample_rate).

11. Audio file I/O
------------------
WAV only. Read 8/16/24/32-bit PCM to float32 in [-1, 1], shape (n, ch).
In-app file dialog (no OS dialog): browse dirs, list wavs, Cancel, Esc.
Save mode: type a filename (TEXTINPUT + Backspace), click existing wav to
reuse name, Save or Enter writes 16-bit PCM. Append .wav if missing.

Open WAV -> original buffer, clears rendered, stops playback.
Save WAV -> writes rendered only.
Render copies original, applies ACTIVE effect only, stores rendered,
plays it. Disabled while Listen or Live Through is on (button greyed,
clicks ignored). Message: "Stop Listen / Live Through before Render."

Play Processed / Repeat: play rendered (stops input stream first).
Original: play original (stops input).
Stop: stop mixer AND input engine.

12. Playback
------------
pygame.mixer, stereo int16. Track playhead as
  (now_ms - start_ms) / 1000 * sample_rate
Return None when mixer is not busy or index past length.

13. Main oscilloscope
---------------------
Below the effect panel; height = leftover window space (min ~90).
1 V/cm with PX_PER_CM = 37.8. y = centery - sample * PX_PER_CM.
Show a trace ONLY while audio is playing, or while Freeze holds a
captured chunk. Idle = grid only, no fake waveform, no wrap-around.
Freeze toggle captures current window. Synchronize: FFT peak 40-4000 Hz,
period = sr/freq, snap start to rising zero-cross. Prefer rendered
buffer if present else original.

14. Audio input (sounddevice)
-----------------------------
Button "Audio Input" opens a modal dialog:
  - List every device with max_input_channels > 0 (guitar interfaces
    included if the OS exposes them). Mark default with "*".
  - Mini oscilloscope of the selected input at 1 V/cm (boosted preview).
  - Input volume slider gain 0.0 .. 24.0, default 8.0. Multiply the
    capture block by gain BEFORE preview, record, and apply_effect.
  - Listen / Stop Listen: open duplex (or input-only fallback) without
    applying the effect; input is also sent to output so the user hears
    the raw boosted signal.
  - Live Through / Stop Live: same stream, apply_effect on each block
    with current knobs/switches/style, write processed audio to default
    output. While live, the host refreshes effect members every frame.
  - Sample / Stop Sample: append boosted blocks; on stop, that array
    becomes original (clears rendered).
  - Close hides the dialog but does NOT stop Listen/Live.
  - Main Stop ends Listen, Live, Sample, and playback.
While Listen OR Live Through is active, Render is disabled.
Starting input shuts down pygame.mixer to avoid device fights.
Blocksize 256, float32, up to 2 input channels, 2 output channels.
If duplex fails, open InputStream and disable live output.

15. Error dialog
----------------
Title "Plugin load failures (N)". Scrollable wrapped list of file +
reason. OK / Enter / Esc dismisses.

16. Robustness
--------------
Never assume plugin Knob has clamp() or click_pts vs clicksPts. Use
getattr helpers. parse_color accepts #RGB, #RRGGBB, named colors, or
(r,g,b). Missing plugin methods fall back to defaults. apply_effect
exceptions surface in the status line.